    "created_at": "2021-05-17T00:13:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-05-17T00:13:19Z",
    "body": "Yea, those files are owned by my user, nothing has changed about them, and they are still usable for aws cli and kubectl commands.\r\n\r\nlol as I was typing this, I figured out what was wrong with the modules. Both came down to weirdness with environment variables:\r\nFor the k8s module, my KUBECONFIG env variable was set to an empty string. I guess kubectl ignores that variable if it is empty. Used `set -e KUBECONFIG` to unset variable, and it's working again. \r\nSimilar story for AWS; I had somehow set the AWS_PROFILE variable in a way that fish's `set` command knew about it, but `printenv` didn't. Running `set -gx AWS_PROFILE=stage` cleared it up.\r\n\r\nSorry for wasting your time, hopefully the next time some idiot bothers you with this question, this may help =]",
